; `gui/common/snap_controls_to_pixels = false`, with the SAME Control chain
; drawn once in the root viewport and once inside a SubViewport.
;
; The one variable: which viewport a Control lives in. Both arms are
; byte-identical four-deep chains of half-pixel offsets, both under the same
; project, so the only thing that can separate them is whether the snap is in
; force where each one draws.
;
; It is not. `Viewport::snap_controls_to_pixels` is a per-viewport member
; initialised to `true` (`scene/main/viewport.h`), and `main/main.cpp` hands
; the project setting to `sml->get_root()` and to nothing else. The opt-out is
; therefore the ROOT WINDOW's alone: Controls inside any SubViewport keep
; snapping however the project is configured. A previewer that reads the
; project setting and applies it everywhere agrees with Godot in every project
; that leaves the default on, and disagrees only here.
;
; WHY FOUR HALVES. `Control::_update_canvas_item_transform` snaps each
; CanvasItem's OWN transform, so a chain of four 0.5 offsets accumulates
; 4 x 0.5 = 2 px of difference between snapped and unsnapped — and both
; endpoints are whole numbers, so each arm's edges land on pixel boundaries
; and neither reading depends on a rasteriser's fill rule. A single 0.5 offset
; would be invisible: floor(x + 0.5) moves a rect by at most half a pixel, and
; a solid rect's own edge coverage rounds to nearest too, so both placements
; cover exactly the same pixels.
;
; Measured through Godot 4.6.3 at the 1152x648 project viewport, with the root
; window reporting `is_snap_controls_to_pixels_enabled() == false` and its
; SubViewport reporting `true`:
;
;   RootArm  Bar unsnapped at 100.5 + 0.5 + 0.5 + 0.5 = (102, 62), so the
;            green square spans x 102..141, y 62..101.
;   Booth    Bar snapped at 101 + 1 + 1 + 1 = (104, 64) INSIDE the
;            sub-viewport, which sits at (400, 300), so the green square spans
;            x 504..543, y 364..403.
;
; Read the pair as one number: the two arms are 2 px apart in each axis, and
; applying the project's opt-out inside the sub-viewport closes that gap to 0.
;
; Both `get_global_position()` calls still report (102, 62). The snap lands on
; the CANVAS ITEM transform and never on `get_rect()`, so only the drawn pixels
; separate the two arms — which is why this fixture measures an image rather
; than a reported rect.
;
; ARBITRATE THIS ONE BY RUNNING GODOT DIRECTLY, not through the 2D reference
; capture. That capture renders the whole scene inside a SubViewport of the
; project-viewport size, so under it BOTH arms are inside a sub-viewport and
; both read (104, 64) — the root window's opt-out is unreachable there by
; construction, and the fixture's whole variable collapses.
;
; The sub-viewport holds Controls only, so its surface is filled by the
; Control-raster pass.

[gd_scene format=3]

[node name="Root" type="Control"]
anchors_preset = 15
anchor_right = 1.0
anchor_bottom = 1.0

[node name="Backdrop" type="ColorRect" parent="."]
anchors_preset = 15
anchor_right = 1.0
anchor_bottom = 1.0
color = Color(0, 0, 0.4, 1)

[node name="RootArm" type="Control" parent="."]
offset_left = 100.5
offset_top = 60.5
offset_right = 300.5
offset_bottom = 200.5

[node name="Link1" type="Control" parent="RootArm"]
offset_left = 0.5
offset_top = 0.5
offset_right = 180.5
offset_bottom = 120.5

[node name="Link2" type="Control" parent="RootArm/Link1"]
offset_left = 0.5
offset_top = 0.5
offset_right = 160.5
offset_bottom = 100.5

[node name="Bar" type="ColorRect" parent="RootArm/Link1/Link2"]
offset_left = 0.5
offset_top = 0.5
offset_right = 40.5
offset_bottom = 40.5
color = Color(0, 1, 0, 1)

[node name="Booth" type="SubViewportContainer" parent="."]
offset_left = 400.0
offset_top = 300.0
offset_right = 700.0
offset_bottom = 480.0

[node name="SubViewport" type="SubViewport" parent="Booth"]
size = Vector2i(300, 180)
render_target_update_mode = 4

[node name="NestedArm" type="Control" parent="Booth/SubViewport"]
offset_left = 100.5
offset_top = 60.5
offset_right = 300.5
offset_bottom = 200.5

[node name="Link1" type="Control" parent="Booth/SubViewport/NestedArm"]
offset_left = 0.5
offset_top = 0.5
offset_right = 180.5
offset_bottom = 120.5

[node name="Link2" type="Control" parent="Booth/SubViewport/NestedArm/Link1"]
offset_left = 0.5
offset_top = 0.5
offset_right = 160.5
offset_bottom = 100.5

[node name="Bar" type="ColorRect" parent="Booth/SubViewport/NestedArm/Link1/Link2"]
offset_left = 0.5
offset_top = 0.5
offset_right = 40.5
offset_bottom = 40.5
color = Color(0, 1, 0, 1)
